# OSS reference-check allowlist — audited carve-out for scripts/oss-reference-check.sh.
#
# Each entry is a  <repo-relative-path><TAB><matched-token>  pair. The path is matched
# exactly and case-sensitively; the token is matched case-insensitively, so one entry
# covers every capitalization of that token in that one file, a public doc included. It
# permits the token in that file only: the same token in another file, or in a file
# whose path differs only in letter case, still fails, as does a different token in the
# same file. Test diagnostics are not allowed by filename; intentional ones need entries
# here too. Entries apply to requirement references (category 1) and task/ADR-id-shaped
# tokens (category 3); a withheld-path reference (category 2) can never be allowed.
#
# Category 1 entries are the req-named identifiers, validation strings, and test
# diagnostics the OSS scrub intentionally left in place: renaming an exported-style
# identifier, error-category string, or behavior-locking diagnostic would change the
# audited behavior, so the worded reason stays in code while the unresolvable tag is
# recorded only in the withheld traceability map.
#
# Category 3 entries are audited false positives: an id-shaped token that is not a task
# or ADR id, such as a CPU architecture name.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
